# Routed model events (revision 1): route.model in the historical audits shows where a step was
# routed, not that the call completed, so these are local e:RoutedModelEvent records with
# e:routedModel and e:routedTask rather than prov:Association with prov:agent and prov:hadRole.
# They can be upgraded to associations once a call-outcome field in each audit is cited.
e:workflow-cvode a prov:Activity ; rdfs:label "Historical CVODE research workflow" ;
    e:evidence e:audit-cvode ; e:startStatus "UNKNOWN" ; e:endStatus "UNKNOWN" ;
    e:routedEvent e:workflow-cvode-event-0, e:workflow-cvode-event-1, e:workflow-cvode-event-2, e:workflow-cvode-event-3, e:workflow-cvode-event-4 ;
    e:interpretation "Audit-to-run/report grouping follows audit task scope; this is a traceability interpretation. route.model records which model each step was routed to; whether each call completed is UNKNOWN because no call-outcome field was checked, so no prov:Association with a model is asserted. Routing applies to the research workflow, not numerical solver execution. No workflow clock boundaries are inferred from route events." .

